<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bismarck Archipelago</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bismarck Archipelago is a group of islands off north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a>, including New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, New Ireland and the Admiralty Islands. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> annexed it in 1884 as part of German New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a>, naming it after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-von-bismarck">Otto von Bismarck</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> occupied it in 1914 and governed it under a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations-mandate">League of Nations mandate</a> as part of the Territory of New Guinea, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabaul">Rabaul</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bismarck-archipelago.jpg" alt="Bismarck Archipelago" width="320" height="194" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA image courtesy Jesse Allen, based on data from the MODIS Rapid Response Team at NASA GSFC · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Newbritain_lrg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
